    id: "p3-04", d: 1, title: "Why Your Body Needs Water",
    text: "Water makes up more than half of the human body, and every system in the body needs it to work properly. Water helps control body temperature through sweat. It carries nutrients to cells and helps remove waste. It also cushions the joints. When people do not drink enough, they can become dehydrated. Early signs include a dry mouth, a headache, tiredness, and dark yellow urine. People lose more water in hot weather and during hard exercise, so they need to drink more at those times. Waiting until you feel very thirsty is not a good plan.",
