    id: "p3-08", d: 2, title: "Military Working Dogs",
    text: "Dogs have served alongside American troops for generations, and today military working dogs perform jobs that machines still cannot do as well. Common breeds include German Shepherds, Belgian Malinois, and Labrador Retrievers. A dog's sense of smell is many thousands of times stronger than a person's, so trained dogs can find hidden explosives, track a missing person, or detect drugs at a checkpoint.\n\nEach dog works with a handler, a service member trained to read the dog's body language and give commands. The two train together every day, and the trust they build is essential in the field. After their service ends, many of these dogs are adopted, often by their former handlers, and spend their retirement as family pets.",
