    id: "p3-11", d: 1, title: "The History of the Bicycle",
    text: "The first bicycle-like machine appeared in Germany in 1817. It had two wheels but no pedals, so riders pushed it along with their feet. In the 1860s, inventors added pedals to the front wheel. Later came the high-wheeler, which had a huge front wheel and a tiny back one. It was fast but easy to fall from. By the late 1880s, the 'safety bicycle' had two wheels of equal size and a chain that turned the back wheel. Air-filled tires soon made rides smoother, and cycling quickly became a popular way to travel.",
